      "page_title": "Aliases: Renaming and Repeating Fields",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rename & Collide"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Alias",
            "Fixes"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`user: viewer`",
              "client naming"
            ],
            [
              "`count: totalRecords`",
              "shorter key"
            ],
            [
              "`kind: __typename`",
              "cache tagging"
            ],
            [
              "`stat: status`",
              "cross-fragment clash"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Two fragments on different types may both select `status`",
            "If the field types differ, alias one or validation fails"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Batching"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "{ a: node(id: \"1\") { ...F }",
            "  b: node(id: \"2\") { ...F }",
            "  c: node(id: \"3\") { ...F } }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Alias bombing",
          "text": "A thousand aliased copies of one expensive field look like a single small query and multiply server work. A real DoS vector."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Depth limiting alone never stops it — depth stays at 2",
            "Cost analysis must count aliased duplicates separately",
            "Codegen erases aliases: the alias becomes the TS property"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "items": [
            "Same response key means selections must merge",
            "Cannot merge? Alias it",
            "Aliases are the escape hatch for repeats"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pipeline",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "lex",
              "parse AST",
              "validate",
              "coerce vars",
              "execute",
              "format"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Parsing is pure syntax: a missing brace fails with line/column",
            "The schema is not consulted at that point",
            "Validation checks fields, arg types, type conditions, cycles",
            "Coercion runs after, failing with a `variables` path error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Validation is the cacheable step",
          "text": "Servers key a validation cache on the document hash. That is exactly why values belong in variables, not the string."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Resolvers"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "resolve(parent, args, context, info)",
            "// info: this field's AST node + path",
            "// lets a resolver see its sub-selection"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "graphql",
          "lines": [
            "fragment F on T { fields }",
            "...F        # spread",
            "... on T { fields }   # inline",
            "key: field(args) @include(if: $flag)"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Execution Internals: Parse, Validate, Resolve",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`ExecuteSelectionSet` walks the AST level by level",
            "Default resolver returns `parent[fieldName]`",
            "Most schema fields need no explicit resolver",
            "Promises are awaited; siblings resolve concurrently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Errors"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A thrown resolver becomes `null` plus an `errors[]` entry",
            "The entry carries a `path` to the exact field",
            "Non-null field? The null bubbles to the nearest nullable ancestor",
            "Worst case it nulls all of `data`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Partial success is normal",
          "text": "`data` with holes plus `errors` is the expected shape, not a bug. Handle both in one code path."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "N+1"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "100 users, each resolving posts",
            "-> 100 database queries",
            "DataLoader batches per tick -> 1"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Trick",
            "Saves"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`@skip` / `@include`",
              "fields before resolvers"
            ],
            [
              "Persisted query",
              "parse + validate"
            ],
            [
              "DataLoader",
              "DB round trips"
            ],
            [
              "Validation cache",
              "full rule pass"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two cheap wins",
          "items": [
            "Directives run at field-collection time",
            "A skipped field costs literally nothing",
            "Persisted: client sends a hash, server looks it up",
            "Request body shrinks to an ID + variables"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Against REST",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "REST",
                "lines": [
                  "N rigid endpoints",
                  "URL-keyed CDN cache",
                  "HTTP status codes",
                  "`/v2/` versioning"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "GraphQL",
                "lines": [
                  "one flexible endpoint",
                  "normalized client cache",
                  "200 plus `errors[]`",
                  "additive + `@deprecated`"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Over-fetching solved: ask for exactly your fields",
            "Under-fetching solved: nest instead of waterfalling requests",
            "You trade HTTP-level caching for client-level normalization"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cost of Flexibility"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The server can no longer predict its own workload",
            "Complexity scoring: a cost per field, times list-size args",
            "Reject over budget BEFORE executing anything",
            "Aliases and spreads both bypass naive depth limits"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
